      "id": "acceptor-coupling/natural-gc/qk-score-diagnostic",
      "title": "Adaptive QK-score decomposition refines natural-donor candidates",
      "summary": "On the adaptive 181-pair, 152-gene train cohort, nominal unadjusted GC-minus-GT score-margin intervals excluded zero for L0H14, L0H5, and L0H3; included zero for L0H4, L1H6, and L1H13; and shifted oppositely for L2H15. This is a selection-QK diagnostic, not a head verdict or claim.",
      "record_kind": "diagnostic",
      "status": "development",
      "evidence_rung": "selection-qk",
      "review_tier": "development",
      "claim_eligible": false,
      "scope": "Pre-softmax L3H1 donor-versus-other score-margin responses to historical arm-specific mean ablations on the adaptively selected train cohort.",
      "first_missing_bridge": "The family was selected adaptively without multiplicity correction; treatment-only clustering omits comparator dependence, arms use different batch-conditioned interventions, execution was dirty and not source-bound, and rows, draws, and checkpoint bytes are absent.",
